    {
     "t": "h2",
     "text": "How to Use Terraform for Effective GCP Resource Management"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "How to Use Terraform for Effective GCP Resource Management"
    },
    {
     "t": "img",
     "src": "https://framerusercontent.com/images/zFjpCa432umkiQukaXGfDqAY7Ss.png",
     "alt": "",
     "w": 1200
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Post",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "Blog Summary"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Terraform is an Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) tool developed by HashiCorp that allows you to define, provision, and manage cloud resources programmatically. Using declarative configuration files, you can describe the desired state of your infrastructure and Terraform will ensure the infrastructure matches that state."
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "Blog Details"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Terraform is an Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) tool developed by HashiCorp that allows you to define, provision, and manage cloud resources programmatically. Using declarative configuration files, you can describe the desired state of your infrastructure, and Terraform will ensure the infrastructure matches that state. It enables consistent, repeatable, and automated deployment of cloud resources."
    },
    {
     "t": "h4",
     "text": "Benefits of Using Terraform:"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Multi-Cloud Support: Works seamlessly across various cloud platforms."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Declarative Language: Describe \"what\" you want to achieve, and Terraform determines \"how\" to achieve it."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Version Control: Configuration files can be version-controlled using Git, enabling collaboration."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Repeatability: Easily replicate infrastructure for different environments (e.g., dev, test, production)."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Infrastructure Drift Detection: Detects and reconciles changes made outside of Terraform."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Cost-Effective: Automates resource provisioning, minimizing human error and saving time."
    },
    {
     "t": "h4",
     "text": "Prerequisites:"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Active Google Cloud Project"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Enable required APIs in the GCP project"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Service Account and JSON key"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Terraform Console with workspace"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "GitHub repositories (CI/CD)"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "In this blog, we will learn how to create Terraform files and manage them in GCP for easier access."
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "1. Create Provider File (providers.tf)"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "In this file, define Google Cloud credentials:"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "provider \"google\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "project = var.project"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "region = var.region"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "zone = var.zone"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "credentials = var.GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Make sure to define the environment variables in the Terraform console."
    },
    {
     "t": "img",
     "src": "https://framerusercontent.com/images/uQwaohVVCskcu7gSAxk3vgxGi0.png",
     "alt": "__wf_reserved_inherit",
     "w": 1200
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "2. Create Main File (main.tf)"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "In this file, define resources needed for your project:"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "# Create a VPC"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "resource \"google_compute_network\" \"network\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "name = var.vpc_name"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "auto_create_subnetworks = false"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "# Create a Subnet"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "resource \"google_compute_subnetwork\" \"subnet\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "name = var.subnet_name"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "ip_cidr_range = var.subnet_cidr"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "region = var.region"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "network = google_compute_network.network.id"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "# Create a GKE Autopilot Cluster"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "resource \"google_container_cluster\" \"primary\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "name = var.gke_name"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "location = var.region"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "initial_node_count = 1"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "enable_autopilot = true"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "deletion_protection = false"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "subnetwork = google_compute_subnetwork.subnet.id"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "node_config {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "service_account = var.gke_service_account"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "release_channel {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "channel = \"REGULAR\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "# Service Account Creation Details"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "resource \"google_service_account\" \"gke_sa\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "account_id = var.gke_service_account"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "display_name = var.gke_service_account_display_name"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "# IAM Binding to assign Kubernetes Engine Admin role to the service account"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "resource \"google_project_iam_member\" \"gke_sa_k8s_admin\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "role = \"roles/container.admin\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "member = \"serviceAccount:${google_service_account.gke_sa.email}\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "# Create Google Cloud Storage bucket"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "resource \"google_storage_bucket\" \"bucket\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "name = var.bucket_name"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "force_destroy = true"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "lifecycle_rule = var.gcs_lifecycle_rule"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "# Create Pub/Sub Topic"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "resource \"google_pubsub_topic\" \"topic\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "name = var.pubsub_topic_name"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "# Create VM Instance"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "resource \"google_compute_instance\" \"vm_instance\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "name = var.vm_name"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "machine_type = var.vm_machine_type"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "zone = var.zone"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "labels = var.vm_labels"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "tags = var.vm_network_tags"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "boot_disk {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "initialize_params {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "image = \"ubuntu-2204-lts\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "size = 100"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "network_interface {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "access_config {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "// Include this empty block to attach an external IP to the instance"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "3. Create Variables File (variables.tf)"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "In this file, define the variables used:"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"project\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The GCP project ID\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"test-staging\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The credentials for the Google Service Account\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "sensitive = true"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"region\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The GCP region\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"us-east4\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"zone\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The GCP zone\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"us-east4-a\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"vpc_name\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The name of the VPC\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"subnet_name\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The name of the subnet\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"staging-subnet1\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"subnet_cidr\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The CIDR range of the subnet\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"10.121.10.0/9\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"vm_name\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The name of the VM instance\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"test-controller\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"vm_machine_type\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The machine type of the VM instance\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"n2d-standard-8\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"vm_labels\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"Labels to apply to the VM instance\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = map(string)"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "\"environment\" = \"dev\","
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "\"team\" = \"development\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"vm_network_tags\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"Network tags to apply to the VM instance\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = list(string)"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = [\"dev\"]"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "# Artifact Registry name"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"artifact_registry_name\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"Name of the Artifact Registry repository\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"test-repository\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "# Artifact Registry format (e.g., DOCKER, MAVEN, NPM)"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"artifact_registry_format\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The format of the Artifact Registry repository\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"DOCKER\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"gke_name\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The name of the GKE cluster\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"test-staging-cluster\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"gke_service_account\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The name of the Kubernetes Service Account\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"test-gke-ksa\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"gke_service_account_display_name\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"Display name for the service account\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"bucket_name\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"The name of the Google Cloud Storage bucket\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"test-bucket\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"gcs_lifecycle_rule\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"Lifecycle rules for GCS bucket\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = list(any)"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = ["
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "{"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "action = { type = \"Delete\" }"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "condition = { age = 90 }"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "]"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "variable \"pubsub_topic_name\" {"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "description = \"Name of the Pub/Sub topic\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "type = string"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "default = \"test-pubsub-staging\""
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Whenever the repositories are updated from GitHub, the actions will be deployed in the Terraform runs section, and you can validate the process there."
    },
    {
     "t": "img",
     "src": "https://framerusercontent.com/images/nr9fuBQswcXwuTpyRHTOAmX0cgk.png",
     "alt": "__wf_reserved_inherit",
     "w": 1200
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Once the run is completed, verify GCP resources are created in the GCP console."
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "Conclusion"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Terraform simplifies infrastructure management by providing:"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "A consistent way to define and provision resources."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Automation that eliminates manual errors."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Scalability and portability across different environments."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "By using Terraform, you can seamlessly manage complex GCP infrastructures while reducing operational overhead and enhancing reliability."
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "status": 200
}